# Line 13 is INSIDE the `for` -- quadratic, fires.
#
# Line 14 (`S := S + 'more';`) sits AFTER the loop and used to fire too. It no
# longer does, and that is the point of the rule's calibration: one
# concatenation executed once cannot be O(n^2) in anything, yet the rule's id,
# its comment and its message all say "in a loop". Firing there was 328 findings
# on drag-lint's own source claiming a cost the code does not pay.
#
# The loop requirement is expressed as "require_ancestor" in the sidecar json,
# because "has an ancestor of kind K" is a property of the path to the root and
# a tree-sitter pattern can only describe a subtree shape.
#
# 22 and 24 are the TStringList alternative the message recommends -- they must
# stay clean, and they are what keeps this from being a test that a disabled
# rule would also pass.
concat-in-loop 13
!concat-in-loop 14
!concat-in-loop 22
!concat-in-loop 24
